{
  "paraphrase": "For every positive integer N, and for every functions a, b, c from Fin N to ℤ, if for every j in Fin N, at least one of a(j), b(j), or c(j) is odd, then there exist integers r, s, t such that the number of j in Fin N for which r*a(j) + s*b(j) + t*c(j) is odd is at least (4*N)/7."
}
